Subject: [PATCH 03326/11362] [outer-loop] arc: wire machine_shape=NvidiaL4
 into the scored submission kernel (operator-directed)

Upgrades the ARC-AGI-3 scored submission to the competition's L4x4 tier (24GB/card, 96GB
total) -- relaxing the dual-16GB ceiling we've been engineering against. Verified correct on
every axis by the operator + a 3-agent verification workflow + the installed kaggle-cli source:

- FIELD NAME = machine_shape (NOT accelerator). kaggle_api_extended.py:4649 reads
  get_or_default(meta,"machine_shape"); --accelerator is only the CLI flag. An "accelerator"
  JSON key would be silently ignored -> default P100 on the scored run.
- VALUE = NvidiaL4 (bare base name provisions the competition's 4xL4, per the T4x2 precedent in
  kaggle-cli#821). NvidiaL4X1 = 1x L4 (rejected); NvidiaL4X4 not in the enum (would 400).
- sm_89 PROVEN: bundled libggml-cuda.so built CUDA_ARCHS="60;75;89;89-virtual"; cuobjdump shows
  native sm_89 SASS + compute_89 PTX -> loads at full speed on L4, no hard-fail. 24GB relaxes the
  VRAM/OOM risk (re-evaluate CARNOT_ARC_MTP on L4).
- Scoring honors the notebook's machine_shape; quota burns 2x (12h run = 24h weekly) -- both
  operator-confirmed.

enable_gpu:true kept as fallback. Ground-truth closer (non-blocking): pull a UI-set L4 notebook's
metadata to confirm the literal string. Optional follow-ups (deferred to respect the explicit
submission-kernel scope): match dryrun kernels to L4 for faithful OOM testing; fix the stale
"built for sm_60" comment in dryrun_kernel/main.py:3; add a post-build sm_89 assertion.

